From f1b85887d6b40c0d5b8238e6546d4924d232db62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:45:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): decode Piano finger contacts in the kernel

Decode mutual-capacitance frames with integer arithmetic in the existing
IRQ thread. Preserve line-noise filtering, multitouch and palm
classification while reporting standard input events directly.

Skip median filtering when the raw signal range guarantees an empty frame
and identical baseline drift. Keep calibration and contact state across
damaged samples. Release contacts on transport loss and rebuild calibration
after firmware resets or suspend. Allocate the raw FIFO only when a
capture reader requests it.

Prevent system resume from enabling IRQs after a failed firmware load.
Initialize resume work before exposing its queue, and stop work and IRQs
before teardown. Restore power-supply state outside the IRQ's touch lock
to avoid a lock inversion.
---
